{
  "title": "What is the CAP theorem and why does it matter?",
  "body": "I'm studying for the CO3040 exam. Can someone explain Consistency, Availability, and Partition Tolerance with a real-world example?",
  "courseCode": "CO3040",
  "tags": "distributed-systems,cap-theorem,consistency"
}

{
  "content": "The CAP theorem states that a distributed system can only guarantee two of three: Consistency (all nodes see same data), Availability (every request gets a response), and Partition Tolerance (system works despite network failures). Real example: during a network split, Cassandra chooses Availability+Partition while HBase chooses Consistency+Partition."
}

